    {
      "id": "bug-038",
      "timestamp": "2026-05-26T14:00:00.000Z",
      "error_message": "SQLSTATE[23000]: Integrity constraint violation: 1062 Duplicate entry 'TEST-9-QF...' for key 'product_variants_sku_unique'",
      "file": "app/Livewire/Products/ProductCreationWizard.php",
      "root_cause": "finalize() is called twice in one wizard session: openPushModal() calls finalize('draft'), then confirmPush() calls finalize('active'). The first call soft-deletes existing variants then creates new ones with SKUs like TEST-9-QF. The second call soft-deletes those variants (deleted_at set) but MySQL unique index still sees the soft-deleted rows — INSERT of the same SKU on re-creation throws 1062. Additionally, product_variants.sku had a global UNIQUE constraint instead of per-product (product_id, sku), which is the wrong business rule.",
      "fix": "1. Removed finalize('draft') from openPushModal() — replaced with autosave() so variants are only persisted once by confirmPush()->finalize('active'). 2. Changed finalize() variant deletion from deleteWithStock() (soft-delete) to forceDelete() after deleting StockMovements and Stocks manually, freeing the unique index slots. 3. Added migration 2026_05_26_000001 to change unique(sku) to unique(product_id, sku) — variant SKUs are unique per-product, not globally.",
